    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0438" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4020: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-03T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                                1921—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 3—9:27
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>310. My 291, August 19th, 1 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d273-f1"/> Wu Pei-fu
                    successes continue, Yochow captured, Changsha threatened. Wu reported planning
                    national convention independent of Peking, Canton. Usually reliable source
                    claims Wu financed by Tsao Kun<anchor n="4" xml:id="d273-f2"/> not Peking
                    government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d273-f1" n="3" xml:id="d273-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d273-f2" n="4" xml:id="d273-f2-content">
                <p>Inspector General of Chihli, Shantung, and Honan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
